CONTRACT solves N×M differently than a serialization library would:
N contracts + M adapters

The schema is declared once, right in the C++ struct:
struct Order {
    std::uint64_t id;
    std::string customer;
    double amount;
    bool paid;

    CONTRACT(Order,
        (id, 1),
        (customer, 2),
        (amount, 3),
        (paid, 4)
    )
};

